<$fill $name="body">

!! What it does

A dock in a corner of the page shows how many things need you. Each count is an //area//: a config tiddler with a filter, for example "tasks overdue", "due today", "started". Click the dock and a panel lists the items. Press an item and drag it sideways: a half ring of action tiles opens. Hover a group (Move, Mute, Status, …) to fan out its tiles, release on one to run it. The item is not opened.

The plugin knows nothing about your data. Areas, extra actions and extra groups are config tiddlers in your wiki.

!! How you use it

# The dock shows one pill per area that has items (alert, then warning, then hint) and the time of the last check. ↻ checks again, and so does every save in edit mode.
# Click the dock: the panel opens. Tabs appear when areas name different tabs. An area shows 5 items, then "+ N more".
# Click an item to open it. The panel stays open, so you can triage.
# Press an item, drag more than 5 pixels (touch: hold 400 ms, then drag). The ring opens on the side of the panel that faces free space.
# Hover a group for 150 ms: its tiles fan out. Release on a tile to run it, or on a group to run its default tile. Esc, release elsewhere, or losing the window cancels.
# The item stays in the panel with a mark ("→ Mon 9", "🔕 until Mon 9") until the next check.
# Click outside the panel to close it. Esc closes it too.

!! Edit mode

Press ✎ in the panel header. The panel switches to edit mode with an //Areas | Actions// switch.

* ''Areas'' — one card per area, grouped by tab. A card edits the area tiddler directly (no Save): caption, level, date field, info parts and the filter, with a live match count. "+ area", "+ tab", ✎ on a tab renames it, drag a card to reorder or to another tab, delete asks twice.
* ''Actions'' — the item list of the normal panel. Drag a row to pin its ring, then click a tile or its ✎ to open the action or group form beside the ring. The settings tab has the same forms with "+ action" and "+ group".
* ''The ring'' — drag a row in edit mode: the ring stays pinned after release, tiles carry a ✎ badge, "+ group" and "+ add…" create new ones.
* ''Esc'' steps back in this order: menu, form, pinned ring, open card, edit mode, panel. "Done editing" leaves edit mode too.

The settings tab lists areas, groups and actions with the same editors.

!! Counts are a snapshot

The area filters run on reload, on ↻, after an action and at the save points of edit mode: closing an area card (header, Done, Esc, opening another card, switching view or tab), leaving edit mode, "+ area", "+ tab", rename, move, delete, and Save/Duplicate/Delete/"↺ Shipped" in an action or group form. They never run per keystroke, so the dock costs nothing while you type. Edit a date in an ordinary tiddler and the counts stay until you check again. The live count on an area card in edit mode (see //Architecture//) follows the filter text while you type; the dock follows when you close the card.

!! Where the configuration lives

|!What |!Where |
|Areas |tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/area` |
|Groups of the ring |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/group` |
|Actions (tiles) |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/action` |
|Recipes (action templates) |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/recipe` |
|Info parts (lines under an item) |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/info-part` |
|Settings |`$:/config/rimir/work-focus/*` (see the settings tab) |

See //Reference// for every field and //Examples// for ready configurations.

